{
  "requirement": "The requirements index MUST show each requirement's evidence state as Valid, Missing, Determination false, FIXME, or Invalid. Valid MUST mean its determination is true and its record passes the same evidence and reference coverage checks as `habeas::validate()`. A false or FIXME determination MUST have its distinct state when the record passes all other checks. The FIXME state MUST pass validation while retaining its distinct label. Malformed or stale evidence MUST remain Invalid regardless of its determination. Each detail page MUST show any validation findings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met, with no acknowledged gaps (no FIXME markers).**\n\n**Implementation (`src/index.rs`)**\n- `EvidenceState` has exactly the five states: Valid, Missing, DeterminationFalse, Fixme and Invalid. `label()` gives the required labels \"Valid\", \"Missing\", \"Determination false\", \"FIXME\" and \"Invalid\".\n- `populate` writes each requirement's or example's `evidence.state().label()` into the index table rows. `render_detail_sections` shows the same state as the evidence badge on each detail page.\n- `LoadedDetailEvidence::load_path` derives the state from the same report that `habeas::validate()` uses.\n  - It takes `inspect_repository`'s `EvidenceReport` and keeps the errors prefixed with that record's path.\n  - In `evidence.rs` every per-record error is prefixed with `evidence/<name>.json:`. This covers schema, requirement text, stale input hashes, reference-set changes, \"no input covers …\", anchor checks, a true example with no `{test}` reference, and \"missing for …\".\n  - A record with no file and no read error is Missing.\n  - A record with no errors is Valid for `true`, FIXME for a FIXME determination, and Invalid if the determination cannot be parsed.\n  - A record whose only errors are \"determination is false\" is Determination false.\n  - Any other errors give Invalid, whatever the determination. A false record with other errors is therefore Invalid, and a stale or uncovered FIXME record is also Invalid.\n  - FIXME records produce no validation error, so they pass validation while keeping their own label.\n- `render_detail_sections` adds a \"Validation findings\" section whenever the record has any errors, including the \"determination is false\" finding.\n- The badge colour mapping and the FIXME references section are presentation details. Other requirements cover them (`index.detail_format`, `cli.fixme_summary`).\n\n**Tests**\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` checks index rows for Valid, Determination false, Invalid from changed requirement text, Invalid from an uncovered `{impl}` reference, and Missing. It also checks the Valid badge on the detail page and that the changed record's page shows \"requirement text changed\".\n- `findings_make_false_and_fixme_records_invalid` covers the boundaries:\n  - a clean false record gives Determination false;\n  - false with stale text, a malformed record, or an uncovered reference gives Invalid;\n  - a clean FIXME record gives FIXME;\n  - a stale FIXME record gives Invalid;\n  - every non-FIXME page shows \"Validation findings\", and the clean FIXME page does not.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs` checks that a valid FIXME record shows `evidence-FIXME` on the detail page and in the index, and that a FIXME record with an empty array, a stale input, or an uncovered reference is Invalid. The FIXME record passes `validate_repository` with no errors.\n- Together these cover the design space: all five states, the false/FIXME distinct-state rule, Invalid overriding the determination, and findings on detail pages. Tests also verify that a stale input hash on a FIXME record is Invalid, though through the status output. The `{impl}` markers on the code that does the work are complete.",
  "references": "32af10e9f1acc3238e0ee16a28d200757007609134ecfd760adcd60ed0eb7e93",
